 "note": "BN-ON1t: r151 b (8 troop impacts, peak frame), r152 a (4 types x 3 frame flipbook + ground mark), r153 a (11 compact steel pieces). Every piece is a 256 x 256 cell at HALF of the 512 master cell; the piece centre = the cell centre (flip frames of one row share it, they must not jump). r = the cell rect [x,y,w,h], content = tight bbox of the opaque pixels, atlas px. Pieces are painted at 65-70 % of the cell: scale so content (not the cell) meets the squad cap (r151 0.55 x squad width, r153 0.7 x). Hit flipbook timing: hit_<type>_1 40 ms, _2 80 ms, _3 120 ms, then mark_<type> stays 600 ms (ground-flat ellipse, tint by branch in code). Colours neutral (steel, bone, earth) except r151 branch accents. | CUT-384 r400 (row y=1280): status marks st_drain_thread (256x~75 strip, trimmed 2 px per end, tile it end to end along the line), st_drain_bead (cluster of 6) + st_drain_bead1 (one bead, 128 slot), st_drain_land, st_morale_up, st_morale_down, st_buff_ring (2:1 ground ellipse), st_heal_burst, st_dazed. Black masters clamped to 0 and alpha-keyed with a filled content mask: safe under normal and additive ('lighter') blend. Pieces at 0.72 of the 344x384 master cell, content centred in the 256 slot. | CUT-400b: st_drain_thread recentred in its 128 strip, periodic (12 px wrap blend), content width 244: tile it end to end at 244 px steps.",
